                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "50671d25-0e21-46e1-835c-b6651eb2f3c3",
                        "source_entry_id": "cbea6264-1a57-3926-9d1f-80e231cf64ab",
                        "source_sense_id": "39770c94-d531-382d-8569-6438ebdad613",
                        "target_lang_word": "thereabouts",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "thereabouts",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2eb7dfb0-8233-3254-9119-0123e218e0c2",
                                        "entry_id": "bd4c9959-9bbd-3971-8a2e-790490f4cde8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of thereabout:",
                                            "About or near that place."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "15794b9a-e84d-461f-8448-fbc47375cfca",
                                                "sense_id": "2eb7dfb0-8233-3254-9119-0123e218e0c2",
                                                "text": "[W]e reſolv'd to put into a ſmall River, which however had a Depth enough of Water for us, and to ſee if we could, either over Land, or by the Ship's Pinnace, come to know what Ships were in any Port thereabouts."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3120e987-bd63-4016-a4c5-5aa4e58584db",
                                                "sense_id": "2eb7dfb0-8233-3254-9119-0123e218e0c2",
                                                "text": "Quite a few minutes would be spun out, for instance, at the smallish town of Chirk, but to me the dalliance was generally worthwhile, except in wet weather, because of the increasing beauty of the wooded hill scenery thereabouts."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8b0c6474-aa77-36dc-bd21-6293139fff4e",
                                        "entry_id": "bd4c9959-9bbd-3971-8a2e-790490f4cde8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of thereabout:",
                                            "About or around that date or time."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f842a48-ea00-46fe-b6cc-e787bf449106",
                                                "sense_id": "8b0c6474-aa77-36dc-bd21-6293139fff4e",
                                                "text": "We ſtay'd by it a quarter of an Hour or thereabouts, 'till the Powder in the Eyes, and Mouth, and Ears of the Idol blew up; and we could perceive had ſplit and deform'd the Shape; […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f713d282-4f3d-36a7-83fd-e571699afd44",
                                        "entry_id": "bd4c9959-9bbd-3971-8a2e-790490f4cde8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of thereabout:",
                                            "About or near to that condition or quality."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3a766e5a-c554-36ec-8e18-b78ee9ca7016",
                                        "entry_id": "bd4c9959-9bbd-3971-8a2e-790490f4cde8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of thereabout:",
                                            "Approximately that number or quantity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "33c5578a-da67-444d-bff7-a63b2cc030a4",
                                                "sense_id": "3a766e5a-c554-36ec-8e18-b78ee9ca7016",
                                                "text": "Fiue or ſix thouſand horſe I ſed, I will ſay true, or thereabouts ſet downe, for Ile ſpeake truth."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "03531651-6518-3b3a-b409-113b42a25506",
                                        "entry_id": "bd4c9959-9bbd-3971-8a2e-790490f4cde8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of thereabout:",
                                            "About that; concerning that."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "abde4ff4-455e-3801-a086-fb5e4c6346bb",
                                        "entry_id": "bd4c9959-9bbd-3971-8a2e-790490f4cde8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of thereabout:",
                                            "Near to that activity or situation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a032d1e7-d0c3-440a-9f71-d3857a28c196",
                                                "sense_id": "abde4ff4-455e-3801-a086-fb5e4c6346bb",
                                                "text": "Cam. [i.e., Canidus.] Our Fortune on the Sea is out of breath,\nAnd ſinkes moſt lamentably. Had our Generall\nBin what he knew himſelfe, it had gone well:\nOh his [i.e., he] ha's giuen example for our flight,\nMoſt groſſely by his owne.\nEno[barbus]. I, are you thereabouts? Why then goodnight indeede.",
                                                "translation": "Canidus. Our fortune [in the battle] on the sea is out of breath,\nAnd sinks most lamentably. Had our general\nBeen his old self, it would have gone well.\nOh, he has given us an example for our desertion,\nMost grossly by his own.\nEnobarbus. Ay, are you near that situation [i.e., also considering desertion]? Why, then we must be at the end indeed.",
                                                "english": "Canidus. Our fortune [in the battle] on the sea is out of breath,\nAnd sinks most lamentably. Had our general\nBeen his old self, it would have gone well.\nOh, he has given us an example for our desertion,\nMost grossly by his own.\nEnobarbus. Ay, are you near that situation [i.e., also considering desertion]? Why, then we must be at the end indeed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "24545455-758d-4459-ac33-087a3cf18d9a",
                                                "sense_id": "abde4ff4-455e-3801-a086-fb5e4c6346bb",
                                                "text": "Cam[illo]. I dare not know (my Lord.)\nPol[ixenes]. How, dare not? doe not? doe you know, and dare not?\nBe intelligent to me, 'tis thereabouts:\nFor to your ſelfe, what you doe know, you muſt,\nAnd cannot ſay, you dare not."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65df7a59-d26e-4b59-8c42-183ca372f80b",
                                                "sense_id": "abde4ff4-455e-3801-a086-fb5e4c6346bb",
                                                "text": "Amid[eo]. […] [D]o not work\nUpon my pity; for I feel already\nMy ſtout heart melts.\nHip[polito]. Oh! are you thereabouts?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
